  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day time and place retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved an exact time, a street line, a numbered-address point, and a public-transport chunk from explicit contexts.">
      <h3>Choose at, on, or in from the intended frame</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Next-day time and place prepositions">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The timetable gives one exact departure: The train leaves <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-hint="An exact clock time is a point, so use at." data-fix="The train leaves at 6:20." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> 6:20.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The map gives only a general street line: The café is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-hint="A general street location takes on." data-fix="The café is on Oak Street." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> Oak Street.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The invitation gives one numbered address: The café is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-hint="A numbered address is treated as an exact point, so use at." data-fix="The café is at 245 Oak Street." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> 245 Oak Street.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The fictional traveler is using public transportation: She is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-hint="The conventional public-transport chunk is on the bus." data-fix="She is on the bus." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bus.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="on" data-hint="Next already identifies the time relationship, so English uses no preposition before next Friday." data-fix="The meeting is next Friday." data-why="Use no time preposition before this, next, last, or every.">
      <h3>Remove the unnecessary time preposition</h3>
      <p>The fictional calendar says, “The meeting is on next Friday.” Tap the one extra word.</p>
      <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">The</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="meeting">meeting</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="on">on</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="next">next Friday.</button></div>
